  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/user/ontologies/2026/7/tea-leaf-diseases-detection/GreyBlight_Disease">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/user/ontologies/2026/7/tea-leaf-diseases-detection/GreyBlight"/>
    <favoredByCondition rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/user/ontologies/2026/7/tea-leaf-diseases-detection/HighHumidity_Instance"/>
    <favoredByCondition rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/user/ontologies/2026/7/tea-leaf-diseases-detection/HighTemperature_Instance"/>
    <favoredByCondition rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/user/ontologies/2026/7/tea-leaf-diseases-detection/LeafWetnessLong_Instance"/>
    <favoredByCondition rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/user/ontologies/2026/7/tea-leaf-diseases-detection/PlantStress_Instance"/>
    <favoredByCondition rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/user/ontologies/2026/7/tea-leaf-diseases-detection/PoorAirCirculation_Instance"/>
    <favoredBySymptom rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/user/ontologies/2026/7/tea-leaf-diseases-detection/BlackFruitingBodyDots_Instance"/>
    <favoredBySymptom rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/user/ontologies/2026/7/tea-leaf-diseases-detection/ConcentricRingPatch_Instance"/>
    <favoredBySymptom rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/user/ontologies/2026/7/tea-leaf-diseases-detection/GreySilveredCenter_Instance"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Dull brown spot expands into a circular to irregular patch, often with faint concentric zoning; centre fades to pale grey or silvered tone inside a darker brown border; minute black fruiting bodies appear as dots. Wound-dependent fungus — favoured by warm, humid conditions with poor air movement and long leaf wetness, but far more serious on debilitated bushes (drought stress, sunscorch, waterlogging, unbalanced nutrition, pest damage aftermath) than on vigorous ones. Attacks via wounds rather than tender leaf directly, unlike Blister Blight.</rdfs:comment>
  </rdf:Description>
